capability keypairs/ed25519  a message signed by an Ed25519 key and checked by its public key (RFC 8032)
  heroes  keypairs.sign, keypairs.verify, keypairs.Scheme
  go      ed25519.Sign, ed25519.Verify, ed25519.PrivateKey.Sign, ed25519.SignatureSize
  rust    ring::signature::Ed25519KeyPair::sign, ring::signature::ED25519, ring::signature::UnparsedPublicKey::verify
  python  Ed25519PrivateKey.sign, Ed25519PublicKey.verify
  note    Linux's `EVP_DigestSign` with no digest: RFC 8032 § 7.1's TEST 1 to 3 signed to their bytes, Wycheproof's 210 cases (117 valid held, 64 invalid refused) on Linux arm64 2026-11-17. On macOS Monocypher 4.0.3's `crypto_ed25519_sign`, and for a check RFC 8032 § 5.1.7's equation computed by the member over Monocypher's point arithmetic (defect 2642, below), a C library the runtime vendors (`runtime/vendor/monocypher/`), since `SecKey` takes no Curve25519 key (`kSecAttrKeyType*` of the macOS 27.2 SDK: RSA and the NIST curves alone) and CryptoKit's Ed25519 signs differently every time, never RFC 8032's bytes (panel 253's R3; decision 2594): RFC 8032 § 7.1's TEST 1 to 3 signed to their bytes and Wycheproof's tcId 10 refused on this Mac 2026-11-20 (`crypto/keypairs/internal/known`, and `keypairs`' own tests). One encoding on every platform (defect 2641): an R or a key whose 32 bytes RFC 8032 § 5.1.3 does not decode (y not below p, or x 0 with its sign bit set) and an S not below the group's order hold nowhere, the member refusing them before either library is asked, since Monocypher decodes y modulo p and takes either sign of a zero x and so held Wycheproof's tcId 151; Wycheproof's `ed25519_test.json` (C2SP's commit 65ca494727a52944c204441c860b039e6786b99b), its 210 cases through this face, then answered alike, line for line, on macOS and Linux arm64 2026-11-21: 117 valid held, 64 invalid refused, 29 acceptable held (its small-order and mixed-order keys), where macOS had held tcId 151. Decided against Go 1.27's `ed25519.Verify`, Python's `cryptography` 50.0.2 (OpenSSL 4.1.0) and OpenSSL 3.5, which hold a signature under a key of such an encoding while all three refuse such an R (each asked 2026-11-21): RFC 8032 § 5.1.3's decoding fails for that key, and two encodings of one key are two keys that check the same signatures; their answer would be the member's check of the key taken away, the R's and the S's kept. One equation on every platform (defect 2642): a signature holds by RFC 8032 § 5.1.7's equation without the cofactor, [S]B = R + [k]A, as OpenSSL checks it (3.5.7's `ossl_ed25519_verify`, read 2026-11-21: [S]B - [k]A encoded and compared with R's bytes), where Monocypher's `crypto_ed25519_check` checks it multiplied by 8 and so held signatures whose R or key has a part of small order that does not cancel, which OpenSSL 3.5.7, 3.5.9 and 4.1.0, Go 1.27.4's `ed25519.Verify`, Python's `cryptography` 50.0.2 and CryptoKit on macOS 27.2 refuse, each answering the 1,757 cases below as OpenSSL does. 1,757 cases through this face, each answer set beside OpenSSL's, 2026-11-21: Wycheproof's 210 above; defect 2642's two, an R with the point of order 2 added under TEST 1's key, and the key whose 32 bytes are zero (a point of order 4), R the identity and S = 0, under the ten one-byte messages 00 to 09; and 1,536 built by RFC 8032's arithmetic, keys and Rs carrying each point of order dividing 8, with a wrong S beside each. macOS before: 674 answered otherwise, none of them Wycheproof's (the first of the defect's held, and under the zero key all ten messages held where OpenSSL holds three, 04, 05 and 08); after, 0. Linux arm64 (OpenSSL 3.5.7): 0 otherwise, its 1,757 answers equal by `diff` to macOS's after; the change does not move its arm (the member's text preprocessed for it is identical before and after). PENDING on Windows: no CNG algorithm identifier names Ed25519 or EdDSA (CNG Algorithm Identifiers, read 2026-11-17); it fails `unsupported` there, never a curve of Heroes' own
